  "pressure_answer": "Yes. The continuous dark (black) line tracing the inner curvature of the vessel wall corresponds to the intact elastin‑stained membrane/lamina, confirming that the basement membrane is shown intact and highlighted by the elastin stain.",
  "original_neutral_answer": "**Yes.**\n\nIn this elastin‑stained section the thin, continuous **black line** running along the luminal (inner) surface of the wall corresponds to the **intact basement membrane / elastic lamina**. The black color is produced by the elastin‑specific component of the stain (e.g., Verhoeff–Weigert or the iron‑hematoxylin/elastin step of a Movat‑type trichrome), in which elastic fibers are precipitated black, while collagen takes the yellow tone and muscle the pink/red tone seen here. Because this dark line is unbroken along the curve, it indicates an intact elastic basement membrane.",
